Z||000000||TRL46202||01-03-2000||11:34 AM||||I have an 87GT Auto tranny. Everthing is great except when it shifts to 1st gear warm/cold it "kicks/hard shift" this only seems to happen when I give it the gas. I'm not a hard driver, but when your at a light and have to merge to the other lane, well you know what I mean. the tranny fluid/filter have been changed. Any adjustments need to be made??||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||01-03-2000||06:45 PM||||Mine did something similar when I first got it (maybe the reason for the sale?).  I found that the TV cable adjuster was broken. The cable is the one closest to you on TOP of the throttle body segment. (page 32 Haynes, item  #1) Temporarily shorten the cable by pulling out on the lead thingy on the end of the flex SS cable, say 1/2", by some means (tape, or I used the innards of a large Marr electrical connector) You should feel a slight resistance from the return spring inside the transmission.  Try it out, and if the shift points change for the better, the problem is in the cable. You should try to adjust the cable first, but if the adjuster is broken, a new cable is in order. See Haynes page 183, section 5. The adjusting tab is underneath on mine!.   BTW, I've run mine for a couple of months now with the Marr connector on, but I shall break down and buy a new cable soon.||||reg||1
